    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If the function <math><mi>f</mi></math>, defined as<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>8</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>,is continuous in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then an ordered pair&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;can be&nbsp;"
